  "name": "Chipmusic (LSDj and Game Boy live scene)",
  "family": "electronic",
  "lineage": "Post-2000 international scene playing 1980s-90s consumer sound chips as live instruments, codified by Johan Kotlinski's Little Sound Dj (2000) and Oliver Wittchow's Nanoloop for the Nintendo Game Boy plus NES/Famicom NSF and Amiga trackers, spread through 8bitpeoples, Blip Festival (NYC, 2006-2012) and micromusic.net — 140-190 BPM patterns programmed step-by-step on four voices (two pulse, one wave, one noise), fast arpeggio 'chords' from single-channel note-cycling, pulse-width and vibrato modulation as the only timbral controls, and a live set played from handheld hardware straight into a PA.",
